      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I don't know anything about the logistics of creating a game so I don't know how obtainable any of these ideas are but I think they'd be cool enough to pay for but not end-of-the-world paywall features.\n1. A new tab accessible by VRC+ users that would essentially be an \"Events\" tab. People could host public events in the worlds they created and they'd show up underneath this tab. Create a new world and want to debut it? Create an event! Having a movie night and want to meet some new friends? Put it up under the events tab! I think being able to put up an hour-long event under a tab would make it easier to connect with new people and also get your new creations spotted. All users (+ and non) would be able to attend these events but VRC+ would be the ones allowed to host them.\n2. Whitelisting/Blacklisting. For a long time, players have talked about needing some sort of moderation in-game but logistically that would be a nightmare so what if VRC+ users were able to blacklist individuals in their own worlds? Then it would be up to the creator if they choose to moderate who they'll allow or disallow in their worlds. To the same effect, for the Roleplay community (as an example), the ability to whitelist the people they allow into their roleplay could help the RP community grow. I guess I got this idea mostly from how GTA RP operates! \n3. Audio Control for individual players. There have been so many times where someone's mic is just too loud or too quiet and the ability to adjust that on our end would be pretty neat-o.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
