      "value": "@{5f4f3828ffa4cb08239b60be|full_name}: VRChat already hosts contests in their discord for events such as the Halloween Spookality event where people can create avatars and there is a winner for the best avatar. A lot of world and avatar creators have discord servers for their avatar creations and such where they can sell avatars and whatnot. They can also host events in their community already if they wanted to. The custom URL thing is kind of cool but I don't think we should pay for such a thing. We already have plenty of world favorite slots and VRChat should've already given us more slots when it comes to avatar favoriting. To the last idea you have. VRChat has already had a way to submit worlds without going through Community Labs. I am not sure if it has been deprecated or not but the way it would work is you would submit your world via a Google Form and from there, an admin would have to check out your world and verify it themselves. This method of world submission is very old, it was used back in 2017-2018, not sure about today in 2020 though.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
